<http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/assertion> {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/delphi-v2-template-counts> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/EvidenceItem> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/delphi-v2-template-counts> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Namespace counts for six Delphi templates, published copies against ontology source, checked 2026-10-31" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/delphi-v2-template-counts> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Method: each published template fetched as https://w3id.org/np/<id>.trig and each source file read at commit 6ba5f9a97a4511c909f5dfd755c7993dd68989f3 of github.com/fractastical/project-delphi-ontology; occurrences (not lines) of the strings \"w3id.org/probknow\" and \"w3id.org/delphi\" counted with grep -o. Checked 2026-10-31. Results: claim, the one published records declare: published https://w3id.org/np/RApE-nGpCMigXqZjeHuYuMJEVTGmTlNTlZl7IcHi_fhdQ has 13 probknow occurrences and 0 Delphi ontology occurrences, while nanopubs/src/04-template-probknow-claim.trig has 0 and 14; claim, the one the current template listing shows (labelled \"Project Delphi claim\", created 2026-10-23T13:08:44Z): published https://w3id.org/np/RAI0QFH7bCNJIeKxwG3EbX5QKyoOjlaESiJkVZKs8iUc8 has 13 probknow occurrences and 0 Delphi ontology occurrences (no source file identified for this one); evidence item: published https://w3id.org/np/RAk4kcX4zA_touv8CeKku9tTUnbR5xiTLSLwFbrKSl3BE has 10 probknow occurrences and 0 Delphi ontology occurrences, while nanopubs/src/05-template-probknow-evidence-item.trig has 0 and 11; provenance: published https://w3id.org/np/RAaYeFYF-Cz2bM5S1wPQsnvs5X6BBxsphL03UkbVZ1lcA has 0 probknow occurrences and 0 Delphi ontology occurrences, while nanopubs/src/02-template-provenance-probknow-extraction.trig has 0 and 2; pubinfo domain: published https://w3id.org/np/RAtKj9bCnB4gUe0E9k-WhffQFSEWd9Ve2hrVllYoLuOB0 has 2 probknow occurrences and 0 Delphi ontology occurrences, while nanopubs/src/03-template-pubinfo-probknow-domain.trig has 3 and 0; rubric assessment: published https://w3id.org/np/RAOAK6Fe6J6JvD4kUCZg53sRpwRkRq7rzFuDtGT7n6Drw has 19 probknow occurrences and 0 Delphi ontology occurrences, while nanopubs/src/18-template-probknow-rubric-assessment.trig has 0 and 21; rubric: published https://w3id.org/np/RAbjeus1yO4SqlPLnpIWNLS6nvW0DGF3879tVduuE0y00 has 10 probknow occurrences and 0 Delphi ontology occurrences, while nanopubs/src/19-template-probknow-rubric.trig has 11 and 0. Three are already migrated in the source but their published copies are not: the claim, evidence-item and rubric-assessment templates. The provenance template is clean in both. The pubinfo-domain and rubric templates are still legacy in the source itself. There are two claim templates in play, both legacy on the network: published records declare the older one, while the current template listing shows the other. The defect is live, not only in drafts: the published record https://w3id.org/np/RAtLFqIIyu4r-GlMcBEfmDtbV-CHwWxQ49gVMtHIX6r48 resolves with HTTP 200 at 5,685 bytes, its own content uses 19 Delphi ontology terms and no probknow terms, and its publication info declares the legacy claim template https://w3id.org/np/RApE-nGpCMigXqZjeHuYuMJEVTGmTlNTlZl7IcHi_fhdQ/template. That record is the published Fisher fundamental-theorem claim from the math-bio-theorems batch: the repository manifest maps the same trusty URI to nanopubs/unsigned/fisher-ftns.trig, published to the test registry 2026-10-30T23:24:44Z and to production 2026-10-31T00:09:54Z. The hub thread pointed at the record, the lean thread identified which claim it is, and both the fetch and the manifest mapping were checked here. The local manifest for that batch records one approver in promotionApprovedBy and a null secondReviewer, so the promotion to production had a single approver; that is a field in this repository, not something checked on the network. On the checking tool itself: nanopub-java's check command exits 0 even when a file fails to parse. Verified here with a file of garbage and with a truncated copy of a real record, both of which print \"RDF ERROR\" and \"Summary: 1 errors;\" and both of which exit 0. The defect was found by the claim-tests thread and reproduced by the lean thread. Every validity statement in these records therefore comes from organism-design/nanopubs/check.mjs, which ignores the exit code, requires one \"Valid (but not trusty)\" line per file, and runs a negative self-test on a truncated record first. Separately, the nanopub-skill assertion-template collection downloaded on 2026-10-31 holds 503 templates and none references the Delphi ontology namespace. Conformance: nanopub-skill's check-nanopub-conformance.py run against records built from v2.0 terms reports every assertion triple unmatched and the required statement st01 missing, for the published claim template and the published evidence-item template alike. The source-versus-published difference was first reported by the lean thread for the evidence-item, rubric-assessment, provenance, pubinfo-domain and rubric templates; it was re-measured here in this clone, and the claim template was added to it." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/delphi-v2-template-counts> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://github.com/fractastical/project-delphi-ontology> .
